WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
There are five hundred million Arabs…

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.950
And yet…

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:04.950
They don't produce science.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.950
They don't win Nobel Prizes.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.450
No Fields Medal, no Wolf Prize.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.450
They don't produce literature.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.450
Look…

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.450
This is the health secretary of the most powerful country in the world,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.950
and he has clearly never opened a history book.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.950
Well, Mr. Secretary…

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.950
let us teach you a little.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.950
There was a time when the whole world came here to learn.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.950
Arab and Islamic civilisation led the world in

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.450
medicine, mathematics, astronomy, chemistry,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.950
optics, engineering, geography and philosophy.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.450
In Baghdad, algebra began with a book by al-Khwarizmi.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.950
And his name… you say it every day without noticing:

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.450
algorithm

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.950
what every device in your pocket runs on.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.450
And when Europe was learning medicine,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.450
it learned it from Ibn Sina.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.950
Ibn al-Haytham

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.950
and al-Zahrawi… the father of surgery.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.950
And Ibn Majid… the stars were his map at sea.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.450
And Fatima al-Fihri founded, in Fez,

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.450
the oldest university still standing in the world.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.950
And you say we don't win Nobels?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.950
Naguib Mahfouz won it for literature,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.450
Ahmed Zewail for chemistry,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.450
and Omar Yaghi won it last year.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.950
Mr. Secretary…

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.450
before you talk about us…

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.450
read about us.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.950
But let's be honest with ourselves.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.950
He doesn't know our history…

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.950
but we've forgotten it too.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.450
Over time… we stopped making things.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.450
And we started imitating…

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.950
Ibn Khaldun said it long ago:

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.950
“The defeated always love to imitate the victor.”

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.950
Our brightest young people went to create for others…

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.450
and our best went to someone else.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.450
And ambition became:

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.450
a degree, a secure job,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.950
and a salary at the end of the month.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.450
And we settled for that.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.450
Today,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.950
a new industrial revolution is being written in front of us.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.950
And the tools are in the hands of anyone with an idea.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.950
But there's a difference between…

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.950
using ≠ making

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.950
present ≠ influential

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.450
And we were influential.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.450
And the people who can bring that influence back

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.950
are here, from the Atlantic to the Gulf.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.950
Just scattered.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.950
So we're bringing them together:

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.950
the ones who build, the ones who fund, the ones who hire,

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.450
in one place.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.450
So the world comes here… to learn.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.450
Our elders used to say:

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.450
When Suhail rises… the night turns cool.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.950
And the question is:

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.450
when Suhail rises this time…

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:26.350
what will we have made?

